SPENDWISE – Test Cases

Test Case| Input / Condition              |     Expected Result
 Monthly budget = 10000                   |     Budget is accepted
 Monthly budget = 0 or negative           |     Invalid budget message
 Valid expense amount = 500               |     Expense is added
 Expense amount = 0 or negative           |     Invalid expense message
 Category = 1                             |     Essentials total is updated
 Category = 2                             |     Entertainment total is updated
 Category = 3                             |     Learning total is updated
 Invalid category = 4                     |     Invalid category message
 Spending exceeds 75% of budget           |     Warning is displayed
 Multiple expenses                        |     Total spending is calculated
 Different expense amounts                |     Highest expense is identified
 Total spending within budget             |     WITHIN BUDGET status
 Total spending exceeds budget            |     OVER BUDGET status
 Remaining budget >= savings goal         |     Savings goal achieved message
 Remaining budget < savings goal          |     Savings shortfall is displayed

Conclusion

SPENDWISE uses basic Java concepts to help students track expenses, analyze monthly spending, and monitor their savings goals.
